AB  - The need to better understand the complex relationships between variables in Ecological Research (ER) has led to adopting advanced methodologies, such as Partial Least Squares Structural Equation Modelling (PLS-SEM). PLS-SEM is well-established in several fields but is only beginning to gain traction in Ecological Research. To ensure best practices, ER studies must rigorously evaluate their use of PLS-SEM. Consequently, this study briefly introduces PLS-SEM and reviews its application in 149 ER studies conducted between 2017 and 2024, analysing 381 models. Compared to established guidelines, the review reveals significant opportunities for improvement in areas including sample size determination, measurement model specification, model assessment, reporting, handling data heterogeneity, accounting for variable interactions, addressing nonlinearity, and exploring alternative plausible models. Finally, this study envisions the growing integration of machine learning techniques with PLS-SEM and proposes a framework for their conjunctive application in ER.
